    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                "word": "tarot",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4234fef3-34a0-43d1-8b65-a3743dd94b79",
                        "entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tarots"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9316a0fa-31e2-3ad4-b7ca-cfb6ad2510da",
                        "entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A card game played in various different variations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "plural",
                            "singular",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6628c0f-bd06-4665-8ab2-3b223bbfad9b",
                                "sense_id": "9316a0fa-31e2-3ad4-b7ca-cfb6ad2510da",
                                "text": "1987, Hans Hahn, “Logic, Mathematics, and Knowledge,” in Unified Science, Brian McGuiness ed.\n[…] it is not that I cannot convince him, but that I must refuse to go on talking with him, just as I shall refuse to go on playing tarot with a partner who insists on taking my fool with the moon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13d33f1d-150a-4dde-bc32-badd9bf915f3",
                                "sense_id": "9316a0fa-31e2-3ad4-b7ca-cfb6ad2510da",
                                "text": "1996, Jan Potocki, The Manuscript Found in Saragossa http://books.google.com/books?ie=UTF-8&hl=en&vid=ISBN0140445803&id=lRbXDsA9u4AC&pg=PA333&lpg=PA333&sig=s0cNY_83AgaK_TWOEA1qpv95tuQ\nThey took me to her and then we all came back to the portal, where we started playing tarot.\nAs we were engrossed in this game, which requires quite a lot of attention, a well-dressed man appeared and seemed to examine us all closely, first one then another."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89570d79-8614-4b77-88f9-f7ec02da9c4e",
                                "sense_id": "9316a0fa-31e2-3ad4-b7ca-cfb6ad2510da",
                                "text": "2001, Donald Davidson, Inquiries into Truth and Interpretation http://books.google.com/books?ie=UTF-8&hl=en&vid=ISBN0199246297&id=hGm9Dj5OmF8C&pg=PA265&lpg=PA265&sig=rjtFvOxVBgk1cro3fLQ5bLn9Eqw\nIn explaining what it is to play tarot we could not leave out of account the rules that define the game; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eacfcbce-d9a0-3691-ba12-af763929a9ca",
                        "entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of the set of 78 playing cards (divided into five suits, including one of permanent trumps), often used for mystical divination."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0f293aa-dbae-48a1-92d8-6e2a11a4e17d",
                        "source_entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                        "source_sense_description": "card game",
                        "target_lang_word": "taroky",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bc93d66b-4984-46ba-af15-e829d66d6257",
                        "source_entry_id": "bfe5a620-2481-3b62-b602-fbfd7c5db86b",
                        "source_sense_description": "card game",
                        "target_lang_word": "tarot",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tarot",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f1fffc7-ba04-36ce-bc8c-e993aeb148bf",
                                        "entry_id": "4969c8aa-e886-3e5f-a97f-a13d81ee6831",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de carte à jouer tarotée et marquée d’autres figures que les cartes ordinaires."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Cartes à jouer"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c26430f7-f29d-4223-a8da-02a9e3911de3",
                                                "sense_id": "9f1fffc7-ba04-36ce-bc8c-e993aeb148bf",
                                                "text": "— Descartes, c'est le type qui a mis au point la divination par le tarot, non ? Je connais un gars, Jasper, qui est du genre à y croire dur comme fer mais, pour être franche, je doute un peu que le tarot permette d'accéder à la vérité éternelle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb8a17de-1560-3f1c-801e-ca2a3c7d3e12",
                                        "entry_id": "4969c8aa-e886-3e5f-a97f-a13d81ee6831",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Jeu qu’on joue avec ces cartes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fc2efe4-111e-43be-aeba-d9a9e4139eff",
                                                "sense_id": "bb8a17de-1560-3f1c-801e-ca2a3c7d3e12",
                                                "text": "Jeannin était joueur et même tricheur, entraîné à cela par un autre ; et insensiblement ils se mirent à tenir tripot, entendez qu'ils attiraient des inconnus à la table de nuit ; on passait du tarot au baccara pendant que nous dormions, et les étrangers étaient plumés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f7887b6-2b11-44fc-a9c8-eaca0df3c21f",
                                                "sense_id": "bb8a17de-1560-3f1c-801e-ca2a3c7d3e12",
                                                "text": "Des joueurs de tarot, jeu de cartes fort pratiqué dans les monts du Jura, occupent habituellement une table d’angle, au fond de la salle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55436714-5ca1-30d9-972d-ecb1514c5ea7",
                                        "entry_id": "4969c8aa-e886-3e5f-a97f-a13d81ee6831",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Le dos d’une carte et plus particulièrement le dessin en taille-douce et ornant le dos des cartes (utilisé surtout en prestidigitation)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
